{"_id":"68a7363c8ec3d8323af1f0e9","nodeId":"o2SH4iQn1Ap2yDZ7cVYLO","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# FLOOR\n\nFLOOR is a numeric function that returns the largest integer value that is less than or equal to a given number. Effectively, it rounds a number _down_ to the nearest whole number. For instance, FLOOR(7.9) would return 7, and FLOOR(-7.1) would return -8.","resources":[{"type":"video","title":"How to Round in SQL","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUXw2JRwCFY","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe6fd"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.508Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/o2SH4iQn1Ap2yDZ7cVYLO.md"}